/* To learn more about Typescript configuration file: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/tsconfig-json.html. */
/* To learn more about Angular compiler options: https://angular.dev/reference/configs/angular-compiler-options. */
/*
 * DELTA from the `ng new --ssr` scaffold: `noImplicitAny: false`, and nothing
 * else. `types` and `include`/`exclude` are the scaffold's own.
 *
 * WHY, and why it is scoped this narrowly. Angular 22 scaffolds no longer spell
 * `"strict": true` — TypeScript 6.0.3 defaults it on, which is what turns on
 * `noImplicitAny`. Frameless-emitted output carries no types at all: the IR has
 * no type channel (IR-8), so a transplanted handler body's lambda parameters
 * arrive unannotated. MEASURED here, on the first real `ng build` this emitter's
 * output has ever seen: with the scaffold untouched the build reports EXACTLY
 * SIX diagnostics, all TS7006, all in `src/emitted/KeyedTodo.ts`, all of them
 * `(todo) =>` / `(item) =>` lambda parameters. Zero template diagnostics, zero
 * AOT diagnostics, zero diagnostics in this demo's own hand-written files. The
 * relaxation is therefore consumed entirely by emitted output; it buys the
 * emitted components nothing they were not already granted everywhere else.
 *
 * This is the repo's OWN standing ruling, not a new licence invented here.
 * `packages/frameworks/react/test/emitted-typecheck.test.ts:14-16` type-checks
 * emitted output with `strict: false` and records the reason verbatim as
 * "deliberate scope, not laxity", citing
 * `docs/goals/frameless-testing-ci-v1/notes/T005-emitted-typecheck.md`. The
 * solid, svelte and vue emitted-typecheck lanes do the same.
 *
 * WHAT IS NOT RELAXED, because this is the task where emitted Angular output
 * finally meets a real type checker and a weakened gate would waste that:
 * `strictNullChecks` and the rest of the `strict` family stay ON, and so does
 * Angular's `strictTemplates` — which keys off TypeScript's `strict`, not off
 * `noImplicitAny` — so every one of the 15 lowered `(click)="onH7Click(todo,
 * $event)"` call sites is still type-checked against its method signature, and
 * every `@for` `track` expression is still validated. That is the coverage
 * T001 and T002 said Angular adds over the other lanes, and it is intact.
 *
 * The narrower alternatives were considered and do not exist: TypeScript has no
 * per-directory `compilerOptions`, and editing the copied output under
 * `src/emitted/` would mean editing the artifact under test.
 */
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noImplicitAny": false,
    "types": [
      "node"
    ]
  },
  "include": [
    "src/**/*.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "src/**/*.spec.ts"
  ]
}
